  "reply": "No, not this month. October ends in two days, and most of SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards is still open. This thread's workstream is empty, so I searched outside it to find the epic. Everything below is read-only.\n\n**Where it stands:** Five items are done, four are in progress and five haven't started. The bars and table below break this down.\n\n**Pace:** Since early September the team has finished just under one item a week. Oriel's chart below works out that at this rate, the 9 open items would be done **around mid-January** (somewhere between late December and mid-March), as long as no new work is added.\n\n**Risks to that date:**\n- **Five items haven't moved in about two months:** SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled, SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout, SYN-99 Save a card for next time, SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step and SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout. Most of them haven't even been updated in that time.\n- **Three open items have no estimate:** SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website, SYN-99 Save a card for next time and SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout. That makes the remaining work harder to size.\n- **Amara Okafor has three open items:** SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website and SYN-92 Show the fare breakdown before payment are in progress, and SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout is waiting to start.\n- SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has been in progress for three weeks with no updates.\n\nIf you'd like to track this epic here, I can create a workstream with the epic and its items in it."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
